    "body": "ITALY - NOVEMBER 8: Ruben Amorim, head coach of Milan, looks on prior to kick-off in the Serie A match between Genoa CFC and AC Milan at Stadio Luigi Ferraris on November 8, 2026 in Genoa, Italy. (Photo by Simone Arveda/Getty Images) Ruben Amorim believes Milan’s comeback win over Olympiacos could be “the start of something”, but warned that his side still have plenty of work to do. With quotes via MilanNews.it , the Milan coach was speaking to Sky Sport Italia and at his press conference after the Rossoneri came from 2-0 down to win 4-2 in Piraeus . Omari Hutchinson scored one goal and set up two more. “It definitely changes our future. We did well in the second half, but we made a lot of mistakes again and we have to improve,” Amorim said. “We have a lot to do to become a very strong team, but the spirit is there. This is the start of something.” The result gives Milan’s Europa League campaign a lifeline. They had won just one of their first four league-phase games, beating Salzburg, before tonight’s victory moved them on to six points. “To believe it, you have to see it,” Amorim added. “Today we saw that we came back from two goals down and won 4-2. Our confidence will grow.” Amorim insisted Hutchinson’s display wasn’t a surprise. “I always expect this from him. He has the potential to do much more. He has talent, like other players in the squad, but it’s the head that counts,” he said. He also played down his own role, despite the impact of his substitutes. “I didn’t chan",
